  << /K [ 5246 0 R ]
     /P 5252 0 R
     /S /P
     /Pg 1074 0 R
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

5248 0 obj
  << /ActualText (The final idea is KAHA\055NI\054 a story machine designed for an art cafe\056 A visitor brings an object\054 something they made\054 found or carry every day\054 and holds it up to the camera\056 They press a button\054 and the machine reads the object as a set of attributes\054 such as its material\054 colour and shape\056 It searches for what each attribute is associated with and lets its meaning drift away from the object\054 toward how it feels\056 From this\054 it prints a short\054 unexpected story\056 With no screen or stored profile\054 the printed slip becomes the only output\056 The visitor tears it off and pins it to a tagboard beside the machine\054 which becomes the installation\220s only memory\056 The installation turns an ordinary object into a small\054 tangible exchange between a person\054 an AI and a printer\056)
     /K [ 8 ]
     /P 5249 0 R
     /Pg 1074 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

